Initial Package Version: 16.2.0
Upstream Status: Not submitted (Fluffy's layout)
Origin: Fluffy
Description: gcc-pass1's dynamic loader and startfile prefix: glibc is
in /sw/glibc, so every 64-bit program it links names
/sw/glibc/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 and its startfiles are found in
/sw/glibc/lib/.  Fluffy's other gccs name every package's lib directory
with /sw/*/lib/ (commit f484394ce3d5 on fluffy/releases/gcc-16.2.0),
which needs that branch's driver commits and so GLOB_PATHS; gcc-pass1
builds upstream's bare releases/gcc-16.2.0 tag and runs against the
build host's C library, which has no GLOB_PATHS, so it is given glibc's
absolute paths, as a patch rather than a commit.

--- a/gcc/config/i386/linux64.h
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/linux64.h
@@ -37,3 +37,7 @@ see the files COPYING3 and COPYING.RUNTIME respectively.  If not, see
 #define MUSL_DYNAMIC_LINKER64 "/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1"
 #undef MUSL_DYNAMIC_LINKERX32
 #define MUSL_DYNAMIC_LINKERX32 "/lib/ld-musl-x32.so.1"
+#undef GLIBC_DYNAMIC_LINKER64
+#define GLIBC_DYNAMIC_LINKER64 "/sw/glibc/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2"
+#undef STARTFILE_PREFIX_SPEC
+#define STARTFILE_PREFIX_SPEC "/sw/glibc/lib/"
